    # self-test log: no gate file changes), the phase's three record pairs (the
    # two corpus samples' reruns and the open record) and two single records
    # (the size record and the API record), by their stems, the check answers,
    # planning's files
    # should any stand uncommitted, the pin of the spec's hash in every sibling log,
    # the pre-P6d bare-shape control, the THREE shape greps over every printed
    # script (and a fourth, PYB, over this script's own source), every placeholder each log prints declared in a root line of that
    # log, this script's own standard output read back for the home directory
    # (specs/0041 ruling I), and this script's own stderr.
    #
    # Usage: m6p4-p3-scan.sh <phase commit> <stage> > <file outside the tree>,
    # where <stage> is "pre-check" or "final". The caller moves the final output to
    # records/logs/m6p4-p3/scan.log. Never prints matched text, an email address,
    # a denylist entry or a pattern. LOGDIR (default records/logs/m6p4-p3) and
    # RECDIR (default records) name where the sibling logs, check answers and
    # records are read from; a dry run points them at stand-ins outside the
    # repository, and the log prints both values and checks them against the
    # defaults, so a logged run with either changed fails.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M2 part 3 P2 from P1's scan script (printed in
    # records/logs/m2p3-p1/scan.log; its change list U to W is there), standing
    # but for these:
    #  X. The phase is P2's: the doc commit pattern and subjects "M2 part 3 P2:
